WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.233
If we bring the left foot here to meet it and bend the knees and then bring the chest back forward you get a nice line in the body.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:44.616
Now it's very important to try this in front of a mirror so you can make sure your shoulders stay forward.

00:00:43.633 --> 00:00:47.066
It's very easy to start doing this.

00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:52.850
This is not the move, this could be a variation of the move but it's not the move.

00:00:51.916 --> 00:00:58.366
We're just twisting the lower body slightly to present our audience with our working hip step.

00:00:57.383 --> 00:00:59.433
Hip.

00:00:58.483 --> 00:01:00.100
Step.

00:01:01.716 --> 00:01:03.083
Hip.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.366
Let's try it together.

00:01:02.383 --> 00:01:03.800
Step.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.366
Hip.

00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:07.633
So shoulders stay square walking forward and step.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:07.983
Hip.

00:01:07.016 --> 00:01:11.083
Feet come together knees line up same direction.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.700
Step.

00:01:11.716 --> 00:01:16.066
You don't want your knees going out here right?

00:01:15.116 --> 00:01:17.833
Step.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:20.483
Knees together lift.

00:01:19.516 --> 00:01:21.033
Step.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:21.500
Lift.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.966
Forward step.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:23.116
Lift.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:23.866
Step.

00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:24.066
Lift.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.616
Step.

00:01:24.633 --> 00:01:26.783
Lift.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.950
Slight angle very good.

00:01:27.966 --> 00:01:33.083
Try it in the mirror it looks more complicated.

00:01:39.616 --> 00:01:45.250
It looks very easy but it's actually it takes a lot of concentration to keep those shoulders forward.
